<resources>
    <string name="app_name">MapMonarchs</string>

    <!--
      PLAYER-FACING COPY LIVES HERE, NOT IN KOTLIN.

      Every string below was a hardcoded literal in a composable. They move here
      so the app can ship in Uzbek and Russian, which it must: the playable world
      is Uzbekistan and shipping English-only to that market is a launch blocker,
      not a polish item.

      MIGRATION ORDER MATTERS. Feature screens are migrated one at a time because
      each screen is a complete unit that still compiles on its own. The DOMAIN
      layer is not: AppError.playerMessage() and Blocker.explanation() change
      return type and every caller must change in the same commit. See
      docs/localization-plan.md.

      TRANSLATION STATUS: English is authored. values-uz and values-ru are
      deliberately absent until a native speaker supplies them, so Android falls
      back to English rather than showing machine-translated copy that would look
      finished and read wrong.
    -->

