    <!-- LOCK COPY. Held as string ids on FeatureLock rather than raw text,
         because a lock is data and cannot call stringResource. Every field
         stays mandatory, so a lock still cannot fail to explain itself. -->
    <string name="lock_territory_why">A territory board — every hex held, with its borders and decay at a glance — is deliberately held back until enough ground is in play to be worth its own screen. Territory lives on the map itself for now.</string>
    <string name="lock_territory_when">Enough ground is held to make a dedicated board worth opening.</string>
    <string name="lock_territory_now">Watch the map. That is where territory sits today.</string>
    <string name="lock_leaderboard_why">A ranking is only meaningful once territory can be won and lost. Ranking players on zero captured hexes would rank nobody against nobody.</string>
    <string name="lock_leaderboard_when">Enough ground has been claimed to rank.</string>
    <string name="lock_leaderboard_now">Nothing to compare yet — no ground has been claimed.</string>
    <string name="lock_notifications_why">Alerts matter once your ground comes under attack often enough to warrant them. The system is held back until there is enough territory in play — and there is nothing to report yet.</string>
    <string name="lock_notifications_when">Territory changes hands often enough for an alert to earn its interruption.</string>
    <string name="lock_notifications_now">Nothing to report yet.</string>
    <string name="lock_missions_why">Missions assign and score objectives on top of the claim loop. They are held back until that loop is proven fun on real walks — an objective bolted onto a loop nobody enjoys would only disguise the problem.</string>
    <string name="lock_missions_when">The claim loop is proven, so an objective adds to it.</string>
    <string name="lock_missions_now">Walk and hold ground. That is the whole objective today.</string>
    <string name="lock_empire_why">Teams and empires are deliberately held back. Alliances built before the solo loop is proven fun would hide whether the loop is fun at all.</string>
    <string name="lock_empire_when">The walk-claim-hold loop is proven on real walks by real players.</string>
    <string name="lock_empire_now">Hold ground alone first. That is the part that has to work.</string>
    <string name="lock_shop_why">There is nothing to sell, and nothing worth buying. A shop opened before the game is good is just a way to take money for an unproven product.</string>
    <string name="lock_shop_when">The loop is proven and cosmetics exist worth owning.</string>
    <string name="lock_shop_now">Nothing here will ever affect who wins ground. Cosmetics only.</string>
    <string name="lock_shop_commitment">Cosmetics only, forever. Nothing sold here will ever affect who holds ground, how fast you claim it, or how far you can walk. Ground is won on foot or it is not won. That rule is the reason this surface is still shut: a store is easy, and a store worth trusting is not.</string>

